From 757d062a5b44a7a5888c765dd2c58291cab67fbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:19:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] WP21: Meta Conversions API sign-up conversion
 (server-side, consent-gated)

Integration with WP18: the WP21 columns (user_account.signup_source, the ad_click outbox columns) and the send index moved into App/app/migrations/0004_meta_capi.sql. config.py keeps WP09's PRIVACY_VERSION 1.6 next to the META_* settings. routes/legal.py and subprocessors.html: one recipients panel (WP09's list); Meta Platforms Ireland is a new recipient_meta_ads entry (EN, CS) listed while sign-up is on and the Conversions API is configured, so WP21's separate panel strings and its duplicate recipients_title were dropped. scheduler.py: meta_capi joins job_intervals (10 min) so the WP10 Operations page tracks it, and the job writes a WP13 run line. admin_funnel.py (WP11) also exports signup_source. New test: the sign-up pages carry no Umami tag (tests/test_umami_guard.py).

Owner decision applied: the Meta event includes client_user_agent. The User-Agent header of the sign-up submit is stored on the meta ad_click row (new column ad_click.client_user_agent, printable ASCII, at most 512 characters) only when the Meta box is ticked, sent as user_data.client_user_agent, and blanked with fbc on every deletion path (withdrawal, purge after sending, failure, expiry, 90 days), and deleted with the row. The consent box and the Meta privacy paragraph (EN, CS) now name the browser type string, so the Meta consent version is ads-meta-v2. 04_legal_positions.md section 6 updated to match. tests/test_meta_capi.py updated, plus tests for UA only with consent, an event without UA, and the privacy wording.
